{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "פנים בפנים", :translit "panim be-fanim", :gloss "faces in faces / face to face"} {:he "פ\"א כפולה", :translit "pe-alef kfulah", :gloss "pe-alef doubled / repeated"} {:he "בפנים מאירות", :translit "be-fanim me'irot", :gloss "with illuminating faces"} {:he "בפנים מסבירות", :translit "be-fanim masbirot", :gloss "with explaining faces"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word repetition: 'פנים בפנים' stated twice in the verse signals two distinct functions of the divine face — illumination and explanation."}], :frame {:text "The phrase פנים בפנים describes direct prophetic revelation; its doubling in the verse is read midrashically as conveying two aspects of that encounter. The idiom is used for Moses' unique prophetic level at Numbers 12:8 and Deuteronomy 34:10, and applied to Israel's collective experience at Sinai in Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael (Bahodesh 9) on Exodus 20:15–18.", :sources ["Numbers 12:8" "Deuteronomy 34:10" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Bahodesh 9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word repetition: 'פנים בפנים' stated twice in the verse signals two distinct functions of the divine face — illumination and explanation.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:25.136763523Z", :model "glm-5.2"}